<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Sigismund, Elector of Brandenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1572">1572</a>–<a href="/years/1619">1619</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Sigismund was Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> from 1608 to 1619. Through his marriage to Anna of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> he acquired claims to the Jülich–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kleve">Cleves</a> inheritance, gaining Cleves, Mark and Ravensberg by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-xanten">Treaty of Xanten</a> in 1614, and in 1618 he inherited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-prussia">Duchy of Prussia</a>. His conversion to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calvinism">Calvinism</a> in 1613 left a Reformed dynasty ruling a Lutheran people.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-sigismund-elector-of-brandenburg.jpg" alt="John Sigismund, Elector of Brandenburg" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous / Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johann_Sigismund_Grunewald.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
